 {
  "area": "Delta summarizer output once the size gate is exceeded (lines 2, 5, 7)",
  "rules": [
   "This program can only ever emit three Delta dicts, each containing exactly one leaf scalar. S1 (line 2, delta1): {\"values_changed\": {\"root['y']\": {\"new_value\": <int args.c>}}} — becomes {} when args.b == args.c. S2 (line 5, delta2): {\"values_changed\": {\"root['x']\": {\"new_value\": <str args.a*2>}}} — becomes {} when args.a == ''. S3 (line 7, delta3): {\"dictionary_item_added\": {\"root['z']\": <int args.c>}} — never empty. Delta drops 'old_value' AND (in the newline case) 'diff', so the leaf dict is always exactly {\"new_value\": X}; the S1/S2 key set never grows.",
   "Empty Delta prints EXACTLY the 12 bytes `<Delta: {}>` + newline. Confirmed for both --b 7 --c 7 (line 2) and --a '' (line 5). The corresponding plain diff line prints `{}`.",
   "SIZE METRIC (gate): size = (sum of len(k) over every dict key in the Delta dict, unquoted and unescaped) + (length of the single leaf's textual form). Print in full iff size <= 100. S1/S2 key sum = len('values_changed')+len(\"root['y']\" or \"root['x']\")+len('new_value') = 14+9+9 = 32, so full iff leafTextLen <= 68. S3 key sum = len('dictionary_item_added')+len(\"root['z']\") = 21+9 = 30, so full iff leafTextLen <= 70.",
